  {
    "episode_id": 81286,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/1/81286.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 2,
    "turn_text": "Okay, yeah, so I was able to catch up with U.S. Representative Mike Gallagher, a Republican of Aloe, the Green Bay area. We talked a lot about what his goals are for his select committee on the Chinese Communist Party. He's going to be the chair of that committee. So I kind of asked him about how that's going to work and everything. And I also asked for some of his thoughts on the war in Ukraine, considering he's a former U.S. Marine. And he's a member of the House Armed Services Committee. So welcome to the show, Congressman Gallagher. It's great to have you on. Thanks for having me. Appreciate it. So to start off with, what are your top priorities in the 118th Congress?",
